from build_magazine import page,write
body='''<section class="library-heading wrap planner-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The practical toolkit · stays on your device</p><h1>See the visit first.</h1><p class="article-dek">A little photo story. A plan you can change.</p><p class="quiet-copy">Choose a place, then edit each step in the words and pictures that work for your family. This is a flexible visual visit plan, not a promise about exactly what will happen or a clinical Social Story™.</p></section>
<section class="wrap visit-builder" data-visit-builder>
<aside class="planner-settings"><h2>Make it yours.</h2><label for="visit-place">Start with a place<select id="visit-place"><option value="">A place of our own</option></select></label><div class="destination-confirm" hidden><p>Changing places will replace the five step descriptions and remove every photo in this plan.</p><button class="button secondary" type="button" data-confirm-destination>Use the new place</button><button class="reset-link" type="button" data-cancel-destination>Keep this plan</button></div><label for="visit-title">Story title<input id="visit-title" value="Our visit" maxlength="100"></label><label for="visit-name">Where are we going?<input id="visit-name" value="a place we choose" maxlength="100"></label><p class="small-note">Use a place name. A person’s full name or diagnosis is not needed.</p><fieldset><legend>Words for a starting point</legend><label><input type="radio" name="voice" value="we" checked> We / our</label><label><input type="radio" name="voice" value="I"> I / my</label></fieldset><label for="visit-length">Starting amount of detail<select id="visit-length"><option value="short">Short sentences</option><option value="detail">A little more detail</option></select></label><button class="button secondary" type="button" data-suggest>Use these starting words</button><p class="small-note">This updates step wording. Your pictures stay in place. Edit any sentence afterward.</p><hr><button class="button" type="button" data-print-story>Print / save as PDF</button><p class="small-note">Opens your browser’s print dialog. Choose “Save as PDF” if your browser offers it.</p><button class="reset-link" type="button" data-reset-story>Clear this plan and start again</button><div class="reset-confirm" hidden><p>Clear your words and local photos from this page?</p><button class="button secondary" type="button" data-confirm-reset>Yes, clear the plan</button><button class="reset-link" type="button" data-cancel-reset>Keep editing</button></div><p class="planner-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><details class="privacy-note"><summary>About pictures &amp; privacy</summary><p>Your edits and selected photos stay in this browser tab. There is no upload, account, tracking or server-generated story. Reloading or closing the page clears your changes. Downloaded or printed copies are yours to look after.</p><p>Choose a photo you have permission to use. Real, current pictures of the entrance, activity, break place and exit can be more useful than a general illustration. We do not invent photographs of a venue. Check all details with the place before relying on them.</p><p>AAC, gestures, familiar objects or other communication may fit better than a printed story. Keep the person’s usual communication available; “no,” “stop,” “break” and “finished” remain real choices.</p></details></aside>
<div class="story-workspace"><div class="story-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Our flexible visit plan</p><h2 data-story-title>Our visit</h2><p>Things may change. We can pause, choose something else, or finish.</p></div><div class="story-cards"></div><div class="choice-strip"><h3>There is room to say</h3><div><span>No</span><span>Stop</span><span>A break</span><span>Something else</span><span>Finished</span></div><p>Use the person’s own words, signs, AAC or other familiar way of communicating.</p></div><p class="story-footer">Made with An AUsome Life · Check the details. Change the plan together.</p></div></section>
<noscript><div class="wrap callout"><h2>A paper version works, too.</h2><p>Write one short sentence for each step: going there, arriving, one activity, taking a break and leaving. Add real photos you have permission to use. Make room for “no,” “stop,” “break” and “finished.” The editable builder needs JavaScript.</p></div></noscript>'''
write('visit-story.html',page('Visual visit planner','An editable photo-by-photo outing plan. Local photos stay on your device; print a plan that fits your family.','/visit-story.html',body,'visit-story-page','<script src="/assets/visit-story.js?v=magazine-20261003" defer></script>'))
